{
  "name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "internal_name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "focus": "High-level component and data/control-flow overview of the Lybra protocol: users and governance interact with proxy-managed configuration, collateral vaults, eUSD/peUSD tokens, liquidation and rewards modules; vaults depend on price oracles and collateral tokens; peUSD\u2019s OFT path communicates through LayerZero with remote-chain contracts. Show module/interface relationships, key asset and message flows, and boundaries with users, external tokens, oracles, proxy administration, and cross-chain services.",
